A `.mtf` file sees exported compile-time constants from its same-directory
module root and compile-time helpers supplied by `@html`.

### A constant capture

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    -- docs/@docs.moth
    export:
        site_name #= "Moth"
    ;
]

[codeblock, $code("text"):
    -- docs/intro.mtf
    # Welcome to [site_name]
]

The compile-time constant is inserted into the Markdown at that position.

### A nested $raw override

[codeblock, $code("text"):
    [$raw: <div>Raw HTML here</div>]
]

Nested templates default to `$md`, but an explicit directive overrides that.
